  "source_review": [
    "The tagged original public legacy declaration forwards MatLegacyFormFieldControlHarness to the same public control/testing class. At original16.2.14 and both advertised minimums21.2.14/22.1.7, the normalized runtime class and abstract public declaration remain identical: no owned state, constructor or methods, directly extending genuine CDK ComponentHarness. Stable public declarations have no deprecated/private/removal/experimental marker.",
    "The exact owned select-base import supplies runtime inheritance; actual owned select module execution retains the genuine marker prototype, inherited root/document locator identities and existing backdrop initializer. Twenty-three constructor/locator/pending/error protocol cases pass per genuine marker class. The exact subclass has no constructor or locatorFactory redeclaration.",
    "The exact owned form-field-base import occurs in four erased generic type bounds. Its actual emitted JavaScript contains neither the marker identifier nor its import. Complete authentic public control/CDK declarations and the actual owned select source compile strictly at all three subjects, with five negative controls. The generic form-field overload fixture qualifies only its marker type bound, not the complete form-field class.",
    "The current legacy form-field public API reexports the unchanged public marker with the exact original legacy alias. Seven source mutations reject runtime value use of the erased import, type-only runtime inheritance, constructor/property interposition, lost inheritance, renamed public alias and type-only alias erasure.",
    "Existing CDK ComponentHarness class-field accessor interposition differences remain explicitly bounded by the readonly public contract and exact subclass guards; this is not arbitrary JavaScript/proxy subclass equivalence. Native selectors, actual legacy Angular views, owned select/form-field methods, packed/floor builds and the complete upstream audit remain open."
